content.text:
Now Contact.astro — dark tile, centered, Apple editorial:

```astro
<section id="contact" class="contact tile-void">  // tile-void? we have --tile-void token; but no .tile-void class. Add? Contact-specific: background var(--tile-void). Define locally with .contact { background: var(--tile-void); color: var(--on-inverse); overrides... } — simpler and keeps in component. OR add .tile-dark-void to global. Contact is the only user; put local overrides in component but via global tokens. Hmm AGENTS prefers global classes in global.css. But a one-off is fine ("组件内只写自己的差异"). I'll give Contact its own bg using tokens local style, with same override block.

Let me define locally:
.contact {
  background: var(--tile-void);
  color: var(--on-inverse);
  --accent: var(--accent-on-dark);
  --accent-strong: #0071e3;
  --border: var(--border-inverse);
  --text-secondary: var(--on-inverse-muted);
  padding-block: clamp(88px, 12vw, 152px);
}
```
content centered with container max-width 640:
- eyebrow centered
- h2: clamp(34px, 5.5vw, 56px) 600 -0.02em lh 1.14; contact-title is split heading + subheading: config heading "有项目想法？", subheading "让我们一起聊聊。". Render heading h2 with <br/> then subheading in secondary? Apple dark tile: title white, subcopy muted. Subheading color: on-inverse-muted.
- CTA mailto btn-primary (auto bg accent-strong in dark? no — .contact isn't .tile-dark class so global `.tile-dark .btn-primary` override doesn't apply. I apply overrides manually: inside .contact set --accent-strong: #0071e3 → .btn-primary uses --accent → sky blue #2997ff with white text (3:1) — borderline. Better set .contact .btn-primary { background: var(--accent-strong); } locally. Or simpler: add a global `.tile-dark-void` class? Adding global class keeps consistency with the rule "components don't copy styles". I'll add `.tile-void` to global.css mirroring tile-dark with bg --tile-void. Then Contact just uses `class="contact tile-void"` and the global `.tile-dark .btn-primary` rule needs updating to cover `.tile-void` too.

Let me update global.css: add `.tile-void` class + extend the btn-primary dark-override selector to `.tile-void`.

- social links: .text-link sky blue.
- section padding. 
- keep contact-inner centered: max-width 620, text-align center; eyebrow margin-bottom 20.

Social list layout: horizontal wrap centered gap 12 28; each link 17px.

CTA margin-top 36. socials margin-top 56.

Also keep `contact-btn` class.

